  "question": "What does Part 5.2 require, and which of our own documents shows that we actually do it?",
  "answer": "I have reviewed the text for **CIP-007-6 Part 5.2**, which is part of the \"System Access Controls\" table (Table R5).\n\nThis specific part requires the Responsible Entity to **identify and inventory all known enabled default or other generic account types**. The identification/inventory can be performed by system, by groups of systems, by location, or by system type [csection-ec458b69bb605a5c345a].\n\nThe standard provides the following as examples of evidence for this requirement:\n*   A listing of accounts by account types that shows the enabled or generic account types currently in use for the BES Cyber System [csection-ec458b69bb605a5c345a].\n\nI have not yet reviewed any of the operator's internal procedures or records to see how they perform this inventory or what their specific identification method is. If you would like me to compare their process against this requirement, please provide the relevant operator document or section.\n\nCited sections:\n- csection-ec458b69bb605a5c345a (CIP-007-6 R5 Part 5.2 requirement and measures)",
